        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0563" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v07-09mSupp/pg412"/>

                <head>158. Memorandum of Conversation, December 28, between Dobrynin and Harriman<anchor n="1" xml:id="d158-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1962-12-28">December 28,
                            1962</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d158-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d158-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Nuclear Testing</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PARTICIPANTS</label>
                    <item>Ambassador Dobrynin
                        USSR</item>
                    <item>W. Averell Harriman</item>
                </list>
                <p>During a conversation at dinner at the Soviet Embassy, Ambassador Dobrynin expressed optimism that an agreement
                    on the ending of nuclear testing could now be reached since Mr. Khrushchev had accepted the principle of
                    on-the-ground inspections. The difference now was only how many.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
